I just called because
they didn't send that check out again.

9
00:02:30,191 --> 00:02:32,902
Oh. I can't believe
they haven't worked this out by now.

10
00:02:32,986 --> 00:02:35,530
I'll make sure they send
another one out today.

11
00:02:35,613 --> 00:02:37,157
I'm so sorry.

12
00:02:37,365 --> 00:02:39,284
Well, what are you gonna do?

13
00:02:41,828 --> 00:02:43,788
So how's your avocado?

14
00:02:43,872 --> 00:02:46,332
It's got two green leaves on it.

15
00:02:47,876 --> 00:02:49,753
I told you, you could grow something.

16
00:02:49,836 --> 00:02:53,214
Well, it was pretty close.
It was life or death.

17
00:02:54,591 --> 00:02:57,594
I'm not kidding.
It could have gone either way.

18
00:02:57,844 --> 00:02:59,179
How's your day going?

19
00:02:59,304 --> 00:03:02,766
My day? My day sucks.

20
00:03:03,183 --> 00:03:04,184
Your day sucks?

21
00:03:05,143 --> 00:03:06,144
Yeah.

22
00:03:07,437 --> 00:03:09,814
Right now I just want to travel.

23
00:03:10,607 --> 00:03:14,611
I'm thinking Chile.
Sounds like an adventure. I don't know.

24
00:03:15,070 --> 00:03:16,571
You ever been to Chile?

25
00:03:17,197 --> 00:03:18,239
Yeah.

26
00:03:18,490 --> 00:03:19,991
You have? What's it like?

27
00:03:20,742 --> 00:03:21,785
Mountains.

28
00:03:22,786 --> 00:03:23,787
That's it?

29
00:03:24,245 --> 00:03:25,705
Well, it was night, I...

30
00:03:26,873 --> 00:03:27,916
It was...

31
00:03:29,042 --> 00:03:30,126
Look, I gotta go.

32
00:03:30,335 --> 00:03:32,087
Okay. Sure.

33
00:03:32,170 --> 00:03:33,797
No, sorry, it's just Gladys.

34
00:03:37,676 --> 00:03:38,718
What?

35
00:03:39,594 --> 00:03:40,929
"It was night."

36
00:03:53,066 --> 00:03:54,401
Hi, Mr. Moses!

37
00:03:55,902 --> 00:03:56,945
Hi.

38
00:05:10,643 --> 00:05:13,021
-Did you start that new book?
-I did.

39
00:05:13,229 --> 00:05:14,647
And, what's it called?

40
00:05:14,856 --> 00:05:17,442
It's called Love's Savage Secret.

41
00:05:17,984 --> 00:05:19,235
Nice.

42
00:05:20,362 --> 00:05:21,488
Is it any good?

43
00:05:21,571 --> 00:05:24,616
It's terrible. I love it. It's awful.

44
00:05:24,908 --> 00:05:28,912
It's about this fashion designer

45
00:05:28,995 --> 00:05:32,832
and his supermodel girlfriend,
and they get recruited

46
00:05:32,916 --> 00:05:37,671
by the CIA to stop an assassination
at the Milan spring shows.

47
00:05:38,004 --> 00:05:41,091
Well, who doesn't like Milan in the spring?

48
00:05:41,216 --> 00:05:42,258
I guess.

49
00:05:43,301 --> 00:05:45,595
Anyway,
I gotta do something for excitement.

50
00:05:46,262 --> 00:05:49,599
My landlady keeps trying to set me up
with her bridge partners' kids.

51
00:05:49,724 --> 00:05:51,559
She just told me she thinks I'm gay.

52
00:05:51,893 --> 00:05:53,103
I try not to judge.

53
00:05:53,228 --> 00:05:57,399
What? Shut up! I'm not gay.

54
00:05:59,109 --> 00:06:00,527
So here's something weird.

55
00:06:02,237 --> 00:06:05,073
I'm actually gonna be
in Kansas City next week.

56
00:06:06,741 --> 00:06:07,992
In person?

57
00:06:09,953 --> 00:06:13,039
That could be a bad idea.

58
00:06:13,957 --> 00:06:15,000
It could be.

59
00:06:20,088 --> 00:06:21,214
You still there?

60
00:06:21,715 --> 00:06:23,800
Yeah. Yeah.

61
00:06:27,303 --> 00:06:29,472
Why don't you call me
when you get to town?

62
00:06:29,806 --> 00:06:31,891
Or... Yeah.

63
00:06:33,184 --> 00:06:35,520
Okay. Bye.

64
00:06:35,729 --> 00:06:37,147
Okay, bye.

65
00:06:40,275 --> 00:06:42,152
Okay.

66
00:06:43,486 --> 00:06:44,612
All right.

67
00:08:26,381 --> 00:08:27,882
{Y:i}Come in, Unit One.

68
00:08:30,135 --> 00:08:31,302
{Y:i}Come in, Unit One.

69
00:08:34,556 --> 00:08:36,266
{Y:i}Unit One, respond.

70
00:10:52,402 --> 00:10:55,989
Don't you know I got to find me a home

71
00:10:56,072 --> 00:11:00,952
Right now in your heart

72
00:11:01,036 --> 00:11:05,248
I'll travel over miles...

73
00:11:05,331 --> 00:11:06,791
Hey, aren't you going to invite me in?

74
00:11:06,958 --> 00:11:08,835
No, I don't think so.

75
00:11:09,127 --> 00:11:10,420
But I bought you dinner!

76
00:11:24,768 --> 00:11:26,269
And you live with your mother.

77
00:11:26,936 --> 00:11:28,021
Awesome.

78
00:11:30,357 --> 00:11:34,235
Yeah, of course. You have no job.

79
00:11:34,986 --> 00:11:39,741
You, mister, are not getting any of this.

80
00:11:42,827 --> 00:11:43,912
Hey.

81
00:11:54,297 --> 00:11:56,049
It's me. Frank.

82
00:11:58,385 --> 00:11:59,427
The avocado?

83
00:12:01,429 --> 00:12:04,099
Why are you here? Get out of my house!

84
00:12:04,432 --> 00:12:05,809
-Hey!
-I told you to call first.

85
00:12:05,892 --> 00:12:07,268
I'm not gonna hurt you.

86
00:12:07,644 --> 00:12:10,772
Would you just listen to me? Please?
Stop that!

87
00:12:10,855 --> 00:12:12,774
Get back. Go away. Stay away from me!

88
00:12:13,650 --> 00:12:14,818
Is that my bag?

89
00:12:17,153 --> 00:12:18,196
Yeah.

90
00:12:18,279 --> 00:12:19,322
You packed it?

91
00:12:19,489 --> 00:12:20,532
Yes.

92
00:12:21,032 --> 00:12:22,367
Did you vacuum?

93
00:12:22,992 --> 00:12:24,577
A little, yeah, it was messy.

94
00:12:24,786 --> 00:12:25,995
Get back. Get out!

95
00:12:26,079 --> 00:12:28,790
Please. We have to leave.
Right now. Stop it.

96
00:12:28,873 --> 00:12:30,375
-Help! Help!
-Hey! Just listen to me, please!

97
00:12:30,709 --> 00:12:32,168
-Someone is trying to kill me.
-Help!

98
00:12:32,252 --> 00:12:33,962
-What are you doing? Listen to me!
-Intruder!

99
00:12:34,045 --> 00:12:36,131
-Help!
-They've been trying to kill you, too.

100
00:12:38,091 --> 00:12:39,551
Why would anyone want to kill me?

101
00:12:39,634 --> 00:12:40,760
Because we've been under surveillance.

102
00:12:40,844 --> 00:12:42,262
They've been listening
to our conversations.

103
00:12:42,345 --> 00:12:43,513
Why?

104
00:12:45,932 --> 00:12:47,350
Because of the way I talk to you.

105
00:12:48,226 --> 00:12:49,227
What?

106
00:12:51,938 --> 00:12:53,189
They know I like you.

107
00:13:00,363 --> 00:13:02,949
Listen to me. Right now. Out the back door.

108
00:13:03,033 --> 00:13:04,534
No way! No!

109
00:13:06,494 --> 00:13:08,496
Don't get me wrong,
I know it's crazy.

110
00:13:08,663 --> 00:13:09,831
Don't think that

111
00:13:10,540 --> 00:13:14,002
I don't think this is crazy.

112
00:13:14,252 --> 00:13:15,837
And it

113
00:13:17,547 --> 00:13:22,302
couldn't be more different than how
I'd hoped to meet you for the first time.

114
00:13:23,511 --> 00:13:25,305
But sometimes things happen.

115
00:13:25,805 --> 00:13:29,184
And I just hope that someday
you and I could be

116
00:13:30,852 --> 00:13:34,731
sitting somewhere, comfortably

117
00:13:35,273 --> 00:13:39,944
and look back on this
as the great, big adventure that it is.

118
00:13:58,296 --> 00:14:00,465
I'm a little hungry, too.
What should we get?

119
00:14:01,966 --> 00:14:03,134
Pizza.

120
00:14:04,177 --> 00:14:05,303
Listen, hon.

121
00:14:07,972 --> 00:14:10,684
Yeah, lots of boys get bullied at school.

122
00:14:14,145 --> 00:14:18,233
I know, but you can't solve it
by intervening like that.

123
00:14:19,609 --> 00:14:21,611
No, I don't agree with you.

124
00:14:29,035 --> 00:14:31,121
I know, it's hard.

125
00:14:32,122 --> 00:14:34,916
I'll talk to him about it when I get home.

126
00:14:39,295 --> 00:14:41,297
No, I should be on time tonight.

127
00:14:46,261 --> 00:14:49,305
Milk, two percent? Okay, love you, bye.

128
00:14:50,306 --> 00:14:51,891
Listen. I can make you rich.

129
00:14:52,475 --> 00:14:53,852
Don't you know who I am?

130
00:14:54,185 --> 00:14:55,186
Of course, I do.

131
00:15:26,676 --> 00:15:28,762
This is off the books. Total blackout.

132
00:15:29,179 --> 00:15:30,597
Yes, ma'am.

133
00:15:32,182 --> 00:15:33,391
There's your target.

134
00:15:37,020 --> 00:15:38,271
Retired analyst.

135
00:15:38,688 --> 00:15:39,773
He was CIA.

136
00:15:40,940 --> 00:15:42,400
Is that a problem?

137
00:15:47,030 --> 00:15:48,156
No.

138
00:15:50,492 --> 00:15:52,869
The spark in your eye sets my soul on fire

139
00:15:52,952 --> 00:15:55,830
Your voice is like a angel above

140
00:15:57,207 --> 00:16:01,378
The touch of your hand, woman
Drives me insane

141
00:16:01,461 --> 00:16:04,881
But, baby, I want to be loved

142
00:16:06,675 --> 00:16:07,801
Sorry.

143
00:16:11,054 --> 00:16:16,184
Wow. If you let me go now,
I won't press charges.

144
00:16:16,267 --> 00:16:18,186
-There's no hard feelings.
-We're way past charges.

145
00:16:19,187 --> 00:16:21,314
How do I always attract losers like you?

146
00:16:22,607 --> 00:16:23,650
I was in the CIA.

147
00:16:23,733 --> 00:16:26,236
Yeah, I bet you were. I'll bet you're a spy.

148
00:16:29,030 --> 00:16:30,156
I have to go see someone now...

149
00:16:30,240 --> 00:16:33,159
You're just gonna make me sit here?
Like this?

150
00:16:33,243 --> 00:16:35,870
You couldn't be safer.
No one knows where you are.

151
00:16:35,954 --> 00:16:37,539
Oh, no. Don't do it.

152
00:16:37,622 --> 00:16:39,374
-Just hold still.
-Don't please. I don't want it.

153
00:16:39,708 --> 00:16:42,293
Sorry, sorry, sorry.

154
00:16:44,045 --> 00:16:45,255
Your eyes are so beautiful.

155
00:16:50,844 --> 00:16:52,053
Want to watch TV?

156
00:16:58,268 --> 00:16:59,352
Be back soon.

157
00:17:03,815 --> 00:17:05,567
Is that thing acting up again?

158
00:17:07,110 --> 00:17:08,862
Oh, hi, Marna, yeah.

159
00:17:11,364 --> 00:17:14,034
Give it a rap, will ya?
See if you could get it going for me.

160
00:17:14,117 --> 00:17:15,785
Of course.

161
00:17:15,952 --> 00:17:18,955
I don't know
why you don't fix this old thing.

162
00:17:19,039 --> 00:17:20,457
Better picture.

163
00:17:21,082 --> 00:17:23,626
-Try a little bit more to the left.
-Okay.

164
00:17:23,918 --> 00:17:25,128
Yeah.

165
00:17:26,671 --> 00:17:28,965
That's just perfect.

166
00:17:34,596 --> 00:17:36,222
Thank you very much, Marna.

167
00:17:43,980 --> 00:17:45,190
Unbelievable.

168
00:17:49,235 --> 00:17:51,029
Should be ashamed of yourself.

169
00:17:58,161 --> 00:17:59,829
It's nice to see you, kid.

170
00:18:00,163 --> 00:18:01,456
It's good to see you, too.

171
00:18:04,834 --> 00:18:07,212
So what's up?

172
00:18:09,047 --> 00:18:10,298
Met a girl.

173
00:18:10,507 --> 00:18:11,841
No.

174
00:18:12,008 --> 00:18:13,009
Complicated.

175
00:18:15,762 --> 00:18:18,723
Got a visit from a wet team.

176
00:18:18,932 --> 00:18:20,809
At my house, 24 hours ago.

177
00:18:22,352 --> 00:18:23,895
Did you ID any of them?

178
00:18:25,230 --> 00:18:26,398
Kinda.

179
00:18:31,528 --> 00:18:33,405
This used to be a gentleman's game.

180
00:18:57,721 --> 00:19:00,557
And you know I love you. Bye.

181
00:19:05,687 --> 00:19:08,314
Independent South African hit team

182
00:19:08,440 --> 00:19:11,276
suspected of killing
a New York Times reporter.

183
00:19:11,651 --> 00:19:14,237
Stephanie Chan. You know her?

184
00:19:15,363 --> 00:19:16,698
No.

185
00:19:18,199 --> 00:19:20,869
Somebody has a serious
hard-on for you, kid.

186
00:19:22,078 --> 00:19:23,163
Yeah.

187
00:19:23,705 --> 00:19:26,291
But why now? I'm retired.

188
00:19:28,251 --> 00:19:29,753
Just have to dig some more.

189
00:19:31,212 --> 00:19:32,630
Watch your back, too.

190
00:19:34,924 --> 00:19:37,635
I'm 80 years old, I got stage 4 liver cancer.

191
00:19:37,761 --> 00:19:40,930
-What the hell can they do to me?
-They can still shoot you.

192
00:19:42,682 --> 00:19:44,100
Well...

193
00:19:46,102 --> 00:19:48,229
I never thought this would happen to me.

194
00:19:49,439 --> 00:19:50,565
What?

195
00:19:52,359 --> 00:19:53,693
Getting old.

196
00:19:55,570 --> 00:19:59,783
I mean, Vietnam, Afghanistan.

197
00:20:02,118 --> 00:20:04,954
Green Springs Rest Home?

198
00:20:08,958 --> 00:20:10,293
Go figure.

199
00:20:22,889 --> 00:20:25,517
So Moses made 22 calls
to Pension Services

200
00:20:25,600 --> 00:20:27,143
and that didn't stand out to you?

201
00:20:29,688 --> 00:20:31,064
Unbelievable.

202
00:20:43,743 --> 00:20:45,161
Hoorah.

203
00:20:48,331 --> 00:20:51,334
Have Endercott intercept the girl
at the Hotel Capri.

204
00:20:51,668 --> 00:20:53,253
Hey, Mike, change of plans.

205
00:21:01,302 --> 00:21:02,470
She's just fine.

206
00:21:02,804 --> 00:21:03,930
I can take you home.

207
00:21:04,014 --> 00:21:05,181
Oh.

208
00:21:06,474 --> 00:21:08,560
I gotta take you down to the station first
to get your statement.

209
00:21:08,643 --> 00:21:11,563
Then there's a couple of federal guys
that are gonna want to talk to you.

210
00:21:11,646 --> 00:21:14,607
I gotta say, I think you're pretty amazing
for breaking free

211
00:21:14,691 --> 00:21:16,401
and keeping it together like you did.

212
00:21:16,484 --> 00:21:18,486
That's impressive.

213
00:21:19,154 --> 00:21:21,322
I'm gonna go back and get my purse...

214
00:21:21,406 --> 00:21:22,907
I can have somebody
bring it downtown for you.

215
00:21:22,991 --> 00:21:24,284
Get in the car!

216
00:21:24,617 --> 00:21:26,536
Let me go! You're hurting me.

217
00:21:33,793 --> 00:21:34,961
Am I gonna die?

218
00:21:35,045 --> 00:21:37,839
No. You just need some sleep.

219
00:21:38,089 --> 00:21:39,591
I may vomit.

220
00:21:41,676 --> 00:21:45,472
This is just like Love's Savage Secret.

221
00:21:52,562 --> 00:21:55,982
I am high.

222
00:21:56,066 --> 00:21:58,068
You have such beautiful green eyes.

223
00:22:23,426 --> 00:22:27,055
You really are CIA.

224
00:22:32,185 --> 00:22:34,854
Officer down.
Corner of North Peters and Conti.

225
00:22:34,938 --> 00:22:37,691
Suspect is a white male, 30s,
black suit and a tie,

226
00:22:37,774 --> 00:22:39,317
driving a black Tahoe.

227
00:23:20,984 --> 00:23:23,653
Freeze!
Put your weapon on the ground!

228
00:23:23,737 --> 00:23:25,447
Put your weapon on the ground now!

229
00:23:28,116 --> 00:23:29,534
Right now!

230
00:23:33,663 --> 00:23:36,833
So you're saying
this was CIA sanctioned?

231
00:23:37,125 --> 00:23:39,961
All right, Thelma, thanks.
I owe you one. Bye.

232
00:23:55,268 --> 00:23:56,978
So it's like that, huh?

233
00:23:57,354 --> 00:24:00,148
Yeah. It's like that.

234
00:24:11,785 --> 00:24:13,286
Where are we?

235
00:24:16,039 --> 00:24:19,292
How did we get to New York City?

236
00:24:23,046 --> 00:24:24,964
I really hate you right now.

237
00:24:25,298 --> 00:24:28,218
I was just hoping you'd be a little
more understanding of the situation.

238
00:24:28,301 --> 00:24:32,263
I was hoping not to get kidnapped.
Or drugged.

239
00:24:32,389 --> 00:24:34,683
I was hoping you'd have hair.

240
00:24:35,642 --> 00:24:38,520
So it looks like none of our dreams
are coming true, at the moment.

241
00:24:38,895 --> 00:24:39,979
Sorry about that.

242
00:24:41,523 --> 00:24:45,068
Thanks for saving me. I guess.

243
00:24:47,195 --> 00:24:48,488
No problem.

244
00:24:48,571 --> 00:24:51,658
Not my best first date.

245
00:24:53,993 --> 00:24:56,329
Not my worst, either.

246
00:24:57,872 --> 00:25:01,001
Until we find out who's trying to kill us,
you're gonna have to stay with me.

247
00:25:02,752 --> 00:25:03,795
For how long?

248
00:25:03,878 --> 00:25:04,879
I don't know.

249
00:25:05,255 --> 00:25:08,049
Whoever's trying to kill us
also killed a New York Times reporter.

250
00:25:09,092 --> 00:25:10,301
She used to live in Chinatown.

251
00:25:24,190 --> 00:25:28,486
Okay. Here we go. Let's come in here.
Right here. Wait a second.

252
00:25:29,112 --> 00:25:30,947
-You just hang onto this tape.
-Oh, no.

253
00:25:31,114 --> 00:25:32,782
No, you said we were just gonna talk to her.

254
00:25:32,866 --> 00:25:34,576
We are. This'll help.

255
00:25:35,410 --> 00:25:37,203
-The woman just lost her daughter.
-I know.

256
00:25:37,287 --> 00:25:39,456
You can't just go around
duct taping everyone.

257
00:25:39,789 --> 00:25:43,043
People are basically kind of decent.

258
00:25:44,711 --> 00:25:46,629
That hasn't always been my experience.

259
00:25:49,966 --> 00:25:51,634
Let me try and talk to her.

260
00:25:52,052 --> 00:25:54,596
-What?
-Just let me do it.

261
00:25:58,600 --> 00:26:00,143
They told me to be patient.

262
00:26:00,810 --> 00:26:03,146
The police have done nothing.

263
00:26:03,313 --> 00:26:08,151
They said it was just a burglary,
but nothing was missing.

264
00:26:08,485 --> 00:26:09,986
She was scared.

265
00:26:11,154 --> 00:26:13,156
We're hoping we can do more.

266
00:26:15,158 --> 00:26:16,951
You worked with my Stephanie?

267
00:26:26,169 --> 00:26:27,879
She sent me this.

268
00:26:29,214 --> 00:26:31,508
I got it in the mail on the day she died.

269
00:26:38,848 --> 00:26:40,183
What does this mean?

270
00:26:40,517 --> 00:26:41,643
I don't know.

271
00:26:41,851 --> 00:26:43,520
I tried dialing the numbers.

272
00:26:44,604 --> 00:26:45,939
Police had no idea.

273
00:26:47,816 --> 00:26:49,693
Where did Stephanie go to college?

274
00:26:52,278 --> 00:26:53,530
Why are we here again?

275
00:26:53,655 --> 00:26:55,782
Those numbers
on Stephanie Chan's postcard

276
00:26:55,865 --> 00:26:57,701
are actually a call number for a book.

277
00:26:57,784 --> 00:26:59,369
Call numbers start with letters.

278
00:26:59,536 --> 00:27:01,705
In the Library of Congress, yeah.

279
00:27:01,871 --> 00:27:05,458
In Harvard-Yenching,
it's a classification for Asian literature.

280
00:27:06,376 --> 00:27:08,003
How could you possibly know that?

281
00:27:12,966 --> 00:27:14,384
You speak Chinese?

282
00:27:37,866 --> 00:27:39,159
Unbelievable.

283
00:27:42,245 --> 00:27:45,248
Hank Maestriano died 2 weeks ago.
Car crash.

284
00:27:45,415 --> 00:27:49,586
Daniel McGinty. Heart attack. Last week.

285
00:27:49,669 --> 00:27:52,130
But if this is a hit list,

286
00:27:52,339 --> 00:27:56,551
why is this guy still alive? Gabriel Singer.

287
00:27:57,927 --> 00:27:59,763
Flies cargo planes.

288
00:28:02,474 --> 00:28:04,142
That's a good question.

289
00:28:14,944 --> 00:28:16,613
Hell of a mess.

290
00:28:17,238 --> 00:28:18,406
Come on.

291
00:28:28,583 --> 00:28:30,043
Joe Matheson, please.

292
00:28:31,544 --> 00:28:32,796
Hold on.

293
00:28:36,466 --> 00:28:37,467
Marna.

294
00:28:38,802 --> 00:28:40,053
Hello?

295
00:29:00,657 --> 00:29:01,658
What?

296
00:29:09,124 --> 00:29:10,125
Joe.

297
00:29:16,840 --> 00:29:20,343
Frank Moses is not a retired analyst
who's never worked in the field.

298
00:29:21,136 --> 00:29:22,804
This guy has a history.

299
00:29:43,533 --> 00:29:44,868
That's a file number.

300
00:29:45,827 --> 00:29:47,787
You need to visit the back room.

301
00:29:48,538 --> 00:29:50,331
You're going to meet the Records Keeper.

302
00:29:58,673 --> 00:30:00,967
I didn't even know this place existed.

303
00:30:01,343 --> 00:30:02,886
It doesn't.

304
00:30:17,484 --> 00:30:19,235
Frank Moses' file.

305
00:30:31,247 --> 00:30:33,249
You gotta be kidding me.

306
00:30:33,750 --> 00:30:37,921
Frank Moses was one of the most effective
black op agents we've ever had.

307
00:30:38,088 --> 00:30:41,091
He retired drug-lords, terrorists.

308
00:30:41,341 --> 00:30:43,343
Hell, he toppled governments.

309
00:30:45,595 --> 00:30:48,723
Yeah. He was truly gifted.

310
00:30:49,724 --> 00:30:51,059
Why was he retired?

311
00:30:51,267 --> 00:30:52,435
He got old.

312
00:30:53,353 --> 00:30:56,648
Then some thumb-sucker came along
and tagged him "RED."

313
00:30:56,731 --> 00:30:57,691
Red?

314
00:30:57,774 --> 00:31:01,778
Yeah. RED. R-E-D.
"Retired: Extremely Dangerous."

315
00:31:02,362 --> 00:31:03,446
Yeah.

316
00:31:03,780 --> 00:31:07,450
Yeah.
They don't make them like that anymore.

317
00:31:10,120 --> 00:31:11,454
Thanks.

318
00:31:13,039 --> 00:31:14,082
I'm gonna need a data haunt.

319
00:31:14,165 --> 00:31:16,668
Every flak he was ever involved in.
Every agent he's ever run.

320
00:31:16,751 --> 00:31:19,629
I want NSA telephone surveillance,
voice recognition...

321
00:31:25,301 --> 00:31:26,803
We have to find Marvin Boggs.

322
00:31:27,095 --> 00:31:29,222
Marvin died two years ago in a fire.

323
00:31:29,305 --> 00:31:32,225
Yeah. Marvin has died many times.

324
00:31:35,103 --> 00:31:36,980
Oh, can we have that one?

325
00:32:01,796 --> 00:32:04,257
All we need is a banjo.

326
00:32:04,341 --> 00:32:06,676
Keep your voice down.

327
00:32:06,926 --> 00:32:08,970
Don't make any sudden moves.

328
00:32:09,179 --> 00:32:11,014
Just stay close to me.

329
00:32:11,097 --> 00:32:13,350
-Don't use your cell phone.
-You took my cell phone.

330
00:32:13,433 --> 00:32:16,436
Don't talk about cell phones.
Don't talk about satellites.

331
00:32:16,519 --> 00:32:17,562
Seriously?

332
00:32:20,690 --> 00:32:21,858
Why are you trying to kill me?

333
00:32:22,609 --> 00:32:23,777
I'm not trying to kill you!

334
00:32:23,860 --> 00:32:24,944
Oh, yeah. You are.

335
00:32:25,195 --> 00:32:26,446
Why would I be trying to kill you?

336
00:32:26,654 --> 00:32:29,074
Because the last time we met,
I tried to kill you.

337
00:32:29,157 --> 00:32:30,367
That was a long time ago.

338
00:32:30,450 --> 00:32:32,869
Some people hold on to things like that.

339
00:32:33,995 --> 00:32:35,663
I'm not trying to kill you.

340
00:32:37,123 --> 00:32:38,166
Okay?

341
00:32:39,709 --> 00:32:41,378
So that makes us friends.

342
00:32:41,670 --> 00:32:42,712
Right?

343
00:32:44,547 --> 00:32:45,548
Right.

344
00:32:45,840 --> 00:32:46,883
Good.

345
00:32:48,760 --> 00:32:50,470
You wanna take that knife
out of my balls now?

346
00:32:55,725 --> 00:32:56,810
Who is she?

347
00:32:57,060 --> 00:32:59,479
Sarah. She's not trying to kill you either.

348
00:32:59,562 --> 00:33:00,897
Yeah. Hi.

349
00:33:01,898 --> 00:33:03,483
I don't stay in the open.

350
00:33:06,403 --> 00:33:08,530
Come on, I'll show you the house.

351
00:33:09,698 --> 00:33:10,907
What's that?

352
00:33:11,991 --> 00:33:13,076
Decoy.

353
00:33:18,123 --> 00:33:19,249
He lives in a car?

354
00:33:23,920 --> 00:33:25,088
Come on in.

355
00:33:34,931 --> 00:33:37,600
Why do you live here
when you have the other place?

356
00:33:39,769 --> 00:33:41,563
Let's put it this way.

357
00:33:41,771 --> 00:33:44,941
When the helicopter passed over
the house last year

358
00:33:45,567 --> 00:33:48,278
and I could feel their eyes on me.

359
00:33:49,279 --> 00:33:52,073
Wet like peaches.

360
00:33:54,617 --> 00:33:55,952
I have a list here.

361
00:33:56,619 --> 00:33:59,080
It was written by a reporter who's now dead.

362
00:33:59,622 --> 00:34:01,791
Along with everyone whose names
are on that list.

363
00:34:01,958 --> 00:34:03,501
Well, almost everyone.

364
00:34:04,711 --> 00:34:07,380
Frank, how many times have I told you?

365
00:34:07,464 --> 00:34:09,632
You cannot trust the system!

366
00:34:09,966 --> 00:34:14,971
I told you when you're in the system,
they switch the flip and you're done.

367
00:34:15,472 --> 00:34:18,767
Man, satellites, cell phones,

368
00:34:19,225 --> 00:34:23,229
chips, net, the web, the dentist...

369
00:34:23,313 --> 00:34:24,481
Marvin!

370
00:34:26,649 --> 00:34:29,778
That list is the one we need help with.

371
00:34:30,111 --> 00:34:32,322
Yeah, I gotta check the files.

372
00:34:33,114 --> 00:34:34,824
Of course you do. Thanks, man.

373
00:34:42,999 --> 00:34:44,501
This guy's insane.

374
00:34:44,793 --> 00:34:49,756
Well, he thought he was the subject of
a secret government mind control project.

375
00:34:49,839 --> 00:34:51,007
This'll take a minute.

376
00:34:51,257 --> 00:34:52,467
Sure.

377
00:34:53,009 --> 00:34:54,594
As it turns out,

378
00:34:55,261 --> 00:35:00,016
he really was being given daily doses
of LSD for 11 years.

379
00:35:00,183 --> 00:35:03,353
-In that case, he looks great. Yeah.
-Fantastic.

380
00:35:03,853 --> 00:35:07,399
Got it. Guatemala. Fall 1981.

381
00:35:08,316 --> 00:35:12,904
Five of the guys on this list were there,
not including us.

382
00:35:12,987 --> 00:35:15,657
San Benito. Just outside.

383
00:35:16,074 --> 00:35:17,158
Injun territory.

384
00:35:17,325 --> 00:35:21,287
Yeah. Was a little village.
Everybody was killed. Civilians.

385
00:35:21,371 --> 00:35:23,123
They told us, "Go in there. Clean it up.

386
00:35:23,206 --> 00:35:25,000
"Make it look like it never happened."

387
00:35:25,208 --> 00:35:27,752
You think everyone on this list was there?

388
00:35:29,379 --> 00:35:30,505
Damn it.

389
00:35:30,964 --> 00:35:32,048
Damn it!

390
00:35:32,549 --> 00:35:34,801
Do you know what's wrong
with this country?

391
00:35:36,845 --> 00:35:38,013
They're all trying to kill us?

392
00:35:38,221 --> 00:35:39,556
Exactly!

393
00:35:40,056 --> 00:35:42,559
Is there anybody still alive on that list?

394
00:35:44,185 --> 00:35:45,645
Gabriel Singer.

395
00:35:45,854 --> 00:35:47,022
Frank!

396
00:35:47,647 --> 00:35:49,858
I never thought I'd say this again.

397
00:35:50,066 --> 00:35:51,860
I am getting the pig!

398
00:35:59,743 --> 00:36:01,369
Who's she talking to?

399
00:36:02,829 --> 00:36:04,080
Just take it easy.

400
00:36:05,081 --> 00:36:07,250
Frank, we gotta get rid of this broad.

401
00:36:07,417 --> 00:36:10,045
I know a great place, just up the road.
Lots of alligators.

402
00:36:10,253 --> 00:36:12,088
We're not getting rid of the broad.

403
00:36:12,339 --> 00:36:14,049
I like her. Okay?

404
00:36:14,549 --> 00:36:16,676
What's the angle?

405
00:36:17,719 --> 00:36:18,970
No angle. I like her.

406
00:36:20,388 --> 00:36:24,434
Okay. So, they pull her voice
from the pay phone,

407
00:36:24,642 --> 00:36:26,102
probably right now,

408
00:36:26,269 --> 00:36:29,356
install the recognition software
and back-trace it to Singer.

409
00:36:29,439 --> 00:36:32,484
So then we show up,
they bring out the satellite,

410
00:36:32,567 --> 00:36:34,569
and we're fried with Y-rays.

411
00:36:37,155 --> 00:36:38,281
How you doing?

412
00:36:39,032 --> 00:36:40,283
Good, fine.

413
00:36:47,832 --> 00:36:51,378
November niner 745.

414
00:36:51,878 --> 00:36:55,006
Singer is going to be in Mobile tomorrow.

415
00:36:55,131 --> 00:36:56,800
We can catch him at the airfreight terminal.

416
00:36:57,175 --> 00:36:58,176
How about that?

417
00:37:07,394 --> 00:37:10,105
{Y:i}The Sunset Limited
with service to New Orleans,

418
00:37:10,188 --> 00:37:14,651
{Y:i}Houston, Tucson and Los Angeles
now boarding platform five.

419
00:37:16,986 --> 00:37:19,072
{Y:i}It's the final boarding call
for the eastbound express...

420
00:37:25,328 --> 00:37:27,163
No, please! No!

421
00:37:27,372 --> 00:37:28,873
You smell like Washington.

422
00:37:29,290 --> 00:37:30,291
Who do you work for?

423
00:37:30,375 --> 00:37:32,836
Coldwell Banker, I'm a real estate agent!
Please, don't hurt me.

424
00:37:32,919 --> 00:37:34,921
No, no. Who do you work for?

425
00:37:35,130 --> 00:37:36,715
-What?
-Who do you work for?

426
00:37:36,798 --> 00:37:37,757
Marvin!

427
00:37:37,841 --> 00:37:40,885
Frank, she's one of them.
She's been following us.

428
00:37:41,094 --> 00:37:44,139
There's a camera in her bag.
I'm gonna kill her now.

429
00:37:44,347 --> 00:37:46,683
No, please don't kill...
Don't let him kill me! Please!

430
00:37:48,476 --> 00:37:50,186
Marvin, just wait, would you, please?

431
00:37:50,353 --> 00:37:51,896
Marvin. Look. Marvin.

432
00:37:53,356 --> 00:37:55,650
No camera in the bag.

433
00:37:56,276 --> 00:37:58,528
Go, ma'am, now. Now.

434
00:38:03,783 --> 00:38:04,951
Get a car.

435
00:38:05,452 --> 00:38:06,703
Try not to kill anyone.

436
00:38:09,205 --> 00:38:11,458
She was following us, Frank.

437
00:38:24,554 --> 00:38:25,805
Sorry.

438
00:38:28,141 --> 00:38:31,728
"She has a camera in her purse,
we have to kill her?"

439
00:38:32,395 --> 00:38:33,813
Seriously?

440
00:38:39,569 --> 00:38:40,612
See you in a minute.

441
00:38:45,700 --> 00:38:46,743
Gabriel?

442
00:38:47,911 --> 00:38:49,496
Right? Gabriel Singer?

443
00:38:51,164 --> 00:38:52,207
What's this about?

444
00:38:52,374 --> 00:38:56,044
Guatemala. 1981. San Benito.

445
00:38:56,127 --> 00:38:57,212
I can't talk to you.

446
00:39:03,009 --> 00:39:04,511
Pair beats ace.

447
00:39:06,930 --> 00:39:08,264
I got one for you.

448
00:39:08,723 --> 00:39:11,851
What did this twice-decorated,
west Texas Jew-boy Marine pilot

449
00:39:11,935 --> 00:39:14,145
say to the Chinese
New York Times reporter?

450
00:39:14,229 --> 00:39:15,271
I give up.

451
00:39:15,355 --> 00:39:18,316
Nothing. I didn't tell her a damn thing.

452
00:39:18,525 --> 00:39:19,859
The reporter's dead now.

453
00:39:20,819 --> 00:39:23,488
And everyone she spoke to is either dead
or a target.

454
00:39:23,697 --> 00:39:24,864
That includes you.

455
00:39:25,699 --> 00:39:26,783
Oh, Christ.

456
00:39:30,745 --> 00:39:33,415
They had me fly this guy out there
in the dead of night.

457
00:39:34,207 --> 00:39:36,376
Hairy little airstrip in the middle of nowhere.

458
00:39:36,960 --> 00:39:40,005
He was CIA,
some dorky little spook in a suit and tie.

459
00:39:40,088 --> 00:39:41,256
Remember that guy?

460
00:39:41,339 --> 00:39:44,050
-Black glasses.
-Yeah. He was giving the orders.

461
00:39:44,134 --> 00:39:46,136
He picked up a package
and I flew him back out.

462
00:39:46,219 --> 00:39:47,220
What was the package?

463
00:39:47,303 --> 00:39:48,638
It wasn't a what.

464
00:39:48,805 --> 00:39:49,889
It was a who.

465
00:39:50,765 --> 00:39:53,101
Frank! Frank!

466
00:39:53,393 --> 00:39:54,811
It's that helicopter.

467
00:39:54,978 --> 00:39:57,105
We're in an airport. So...

468
00:39:57,272 --> 00:39:58,815
It's the same helicopter.

469
00:39:59,357 --> 00:40:04,320
November niner 748 Charlie.

470
00:40:04,571 --> 00:40:08,241
November niner 748 Charlie.

471
00:40:09,034 --> 00:40:12,787
See? Frank, November niner 748...

472
00:40:12,871 --> 00:40:13,913
Is that a 4?

473
00:40:13,997 --> 00:40:15,331
This is a 4. Charlie.

474
00:40:15,540 --> 00:40:17,459
Is that a 7? What is that?

475
00:40:17,542 --> 00:40:19,085
I'll tell you what it is.

476
00:40:28,386 --> 00:40:31,222
I told you she shouldn't
have made that phone call!

477
00:40:33,266 --> 00:40:34,351
We lost visual on target.

478
00:40:34,434 --> 00:40:35,935
All right. Shake the tree.

479
00:40:36,019 --> 00:40:38,271
-You'll pay for the breakage?
-Yeah, Roger that.

480
00:41:00,335 --> 00:41:02,128
That's right, old man!

481
00:41:03,838 --> 00:41:06,174
-Old man?
-No respect.

482
00:41:06,383 --> 00:41:07,425
Can I kill her now?

483
00:41:18,687 --> 00:41:20,063
She called me an old man.

484
00:41:22,232 --> 00:41:24,025
Pig! Open the pig!

485
00:41:30,240 --> 00:41:31,241
Okay.

486
00:41:42,919 --> 00:41:44,087
Grenade!

487
00:41:47,507 --> 00:41:48,925
Damn satellites!

488
00:41:50,010 --> 00:41:51,302
Boop to that!

489
00:41:54,639 --> 00:41:57,058
Yeah, you just stay right there.

490
00:41:57,183 --> 00:41:58,226
This is gonna be good.

491
00:42:14,284 --> 00:42:15,869
-You okay?
-Yeah.

492
00:42:17,037 --> 00:42:20,123
Come on, come on. Hey. All right?

493
00:42:21,541 --> 00:42:22,584
What are you doing?

494
00:42:59,496 --> 00:43:01,206
Old man, my ass.

495
00:43:01,373 --> 00:43:02,374
God damn it!

496
00:43:03,291 --> 00:43:06,169
-Smoke and thermals. Obstructed view.
-Signal's fading.

497
00:43:08,797 --> 00:43:10,173
Nice shot.

498
00:43:10,799 --> 00:43:13,051
-Thanks.
-We should get out of here.

499
00:43:31,861 --> 00:43:35,323
You really know how to show a girl
a good time, Frank.

500
00:43:35,407 --> 00:43:37,033
I will kill you, Marvin.

501
00:43:38,034 --> 00:43:41,871
Take it easy, man. She likes you.

502
00:43:48,086 --> 00:43:49,504
How can you tell?

503
00:43:51,631 --> 00:43:54,175
Notice how she sticks around?

504
00:43:54,342 --> 00:43:57,595
'Cause if women don't like you,
they don't stick around.

505
00:43:57,887 --> 00:44:00,056
She doesn't have much of a choice.
Does she?

506
00:44:00,390 --> 00:44:01,599
Sure she does.

507
00:44:03,268 --> 00:44:04,894
Really?

508
00:44:05,520 --> 00:44:06,730
You think so?

509
00:44:12,027 --> 00:44:14,154
You know, if it is the CIA,

510
00:44:15,238 --> 00:44:17,532
then there's only one place that we can go

511
00:44:17,615 --> 00:44:19,743
to find out why they're coming after us.

512
00:44:19,826 --> 00:44:20,869
Yeah.

513
00:44:21,077 --> 00:44:23,288
We're gonna get killed there, for sure.

514
00:44:24,247 --> 00:44:25,331
In or out?

515
00:44:25,415 --> 00:44:28,293
No. Of course I'm in. I'm just saying.

516
00:44:31,421 --> 00:44:33,423
We're gonna need some serious help.

517
00:44:36,009 --> 00:44:39,596
This is not the kind of help I meant, Frank.

518
00:44:41,097 --> 00:44:43,391
You're not actually gonna go in there,
are you?

519
00:44:46,102 --> 00:44:47,645
I don't think I can go, Frank.

520
00:44:47,729 --> 00:44:51,941
The last time they put some electrical wires

521
00:44:52,025 --> 00:44:54,235
in some not very nice places.

522
00:44:59,282 --> 00:45:01,326
Listen, hang onto that for me.

523
00:45:04,829 --> 00:45:06,247
I'll be right back.

524
00:45:14,339 --> 00:45:15,340
Hey.

525
00:45:17,133 --> 00:45:18,176
Be careful.

526
00:45:43,618 --> 00:45:47,664
Tell Ivan Simanov that Frank Moses is...

527
00:45:47,747 --> 00:45:49,874
Frank Moses is here to see him.

528
00:46:04,180 --> 00:46:06,307
I have to say...

529
00:46:06,683 --> 00:46:11,062
this is the last thing I expected

530
00:46:11,312 --> 00:46:14,149
when I got up this morning.

531
00:46:19,696 --> 00:46:23,616
I have many times dreamed of killing you.

532
00:46:25,118 --> 00:46:26,453
But now...

533
00:46:30,415 --> 00:46:32,334
you are...

534
00:46:33,710 --> 00:46:35,628
a pensioner.

535
00:46:36,880 --> 00:46:38,590
Couple of years now.

536
00:46:38,965 --> 00:46:40,717
Time passes.

537
00:46:41,176 --> 00:46:44,596
As we get older,
things seem less important.

538
00:46:45,930 --> 00:46:47,265
Still

539
00:46:49,976 --> 00:46:51,561
I owe you

540
00:46:51,978 --> 00:46:54,064
for killing Igor.

541
00:46:54,481 --> 00:46:56,524
-Igor the Butcher.
-He was a great asset.

542
00:46:56,608 --> 00:46:59,611
-He was a pig.
-He was my cousin.

543
00:47:00,862 --> 00:47:01,905
I'm sorry.

544
00:47:12,791 --> 00:47:14,084
To Igor.

545
00:47:15,001 --> 00:47:16,419
The Butcher.

546
00:47:17,587 --> 00:47:18,922
He's not dead.

547
00:47:21,758 --> 00:47:22,842
I flipped him.

548
00:47:23,885 --> 00:47:24,969
No.

549
00:47:25,136 --> 00:47:27,389
He owns a string of 7-Elevens
in Orange County.

550
00:47:28,640 --> 00:47:29,849
He weighs 500 pounds.

551
00:47:43,363 --> 00:47:44,447
Drink.

552
00:47:45,615 --> 00:47:47,033
Who are we drinking to now?

553
00:47:48,410 --> 00:47:49,619
Veronique.

554
00:47:51,454 --> 00:47:54,165
She was mine.

555
00:47:55,291 --> 00:47:56,960
-Impossible.
-Yes!

556
00:48:05,051 --> 00:48:06,636
Whatever she got, it was worth it.

557
00:48:11,349 --> 00:48:12,684
I miss the old days.

558
00:48:16,771 --> 00:48:20,650
I haven't killed anyone in years.

559
00:48:22,527 --> 00:48:23,778
That's sad.

560
00:48:29,034 --> 00:48:30,160
But

561
00:48:31,536 --> 00:48:34,664
I think you are not here for the vodka.

562
00:48:39,294 --> 00:48:41,212
I'm going to break into the CIA.

563
00:48:42,464 --> 00:48:44,924
I need your complete
security layout of Langley.

564
00:48:45,508 --> 00:48:48,678
Cracks. Codes. ID swipes.

565
00:48:49,679 --> 00:48:50,764
All of it.

566
00:48:52,849 --> 00:48:55,935
Amusing as this would be,

567
00:48:56,895 --> 00:48:59,939
it is beyond my reach.

568
00:49:07,155 --> 00:49:10,325
A favor from Frank Moses?

569
00:49:20,877 --> 00:49:23,296
I can't believe you're actually
letting me come along.

570
00:49:23,922 --> 00:49:26,966
The badges Ivan gave us
are for a General Harlow

571
00:49:27,050 --> 00:49:30,178
and a female nuclear physicist
from Los Alamos.

572
00:49:33,014 --> 00:49:34,432
Sheniqua Johnson?

573
00:49:35,350 --> 00:49:36,434
You're adopted.

574
00:49:36,643 --> 00:49:37,769
Okay.

575
00:49:41,815 --> 00:49:44,234
This is so cool.

576
00:50:02,669 --> 00:50:03,712
What?

577
00:50:04,087 --> 00:50:06,256
I dropped it.

578
00:50:08,842 --> 00:50:10,176
Freeze!

579
00:50:13,847 --> 00:50:16,266
The General has dropped his contact lens.

580
00:50:18,351 --> 00:50:20,353
Perhaps you'd like to help us?

581
00:50:22,397 --> 00:50:23,857
Sorry.

582
00:50:30,238 --> 00:50:32,657
Found it! I found it!

583
00:50:33,700 --> 00:50:35,243
I found it.

584
00:50:48,798 --> 00:50:50,342
Have a good day, sir.

585
00:50:50,842 --> 00:50:52,093
Gentlemen.

586
00:50:52,969 --> 00:50:54,304
My God!

587
00:50:56,556 --> 00:51:00,226
What do you suppose the punishment
is for what we're doing here?

588
00:51:00,810 --> 00:51:02,145
Death.

589
00:51:03,480 --> 00:51:04,647
Maybe life in prison.

590
00:51:04,856 --> 00:51:06,232
Awesome.

591
00:51:13,031 --> 00:51:14,824
Why are you holding that button?

592
00:51:25,001 --> 00:51:26,586
The Russians give you the code?

593
00:51:27,128 --> 00:51:28,213
No.

594
00:51:29,422 --> 00:51:31,424
Changes every six hours.

595
00:51:31,841 --> 00:51:33,134
Will you hold that for me for a second?

596
00:51:33,218 --> 00:51:34,219
Yeah.

597
00:51:37,722 --> 00:51:39,182
It's unbreakable.

598
00:51:42,310 --> 00:51:43,728
Wow.

599
00:51:47,691 --> 00:51:48,858
Come on.

600
00:52:02,497 --> 00:52:03,957
Mr. Moses!

601
00:52:05,208 --> 00:52:07,002
Been a long time.

602
00:52:07,377 --> 00:52:09,504
I'm gonna need to see that Guatemala file.

603
00:52:09,879 --> 00:52:11,006
Guatemala?

604
00:52:11,506 --> 00:52:12,966
Yes.

605
00:52:14,175 --> 00:52:15,552
I think I can help you.

606
00:52:16,720 --> 00:52:17,846
Great.

607
00:52:22,100 --> 00:52:25,061
It's been a whole new world
around here since you left.

608
00:52:27,105 --> 00:52:28,231
Guatemala.

609
00:52:32,902 --> 00:52:34,112
You know, you're gonna catch hell for this.

610
00:52:34,279 --> 00:52:35,822
After what I've seen?

611
00:52:38,241 --> 00:52:39,743
Oh, I should tell you,

612
00:52:40,035 --> 00:52:43,204
there's a new guy came down here
yesterday looking for your file.

613
00:52:43,413 --> 00:52:46,124
Name of William Cooper?

614
00:52:47,042 --> 00:52:49,252
6'1"? Cute hair?

615
00:52:50,420 --> 00:52:51,546
Hair was cute.

616
00:52:52,922 --> 00:52:55,008
But I thought he looked a little tough,
though.

617
00:52:58,386 --> 00:52:59,929
You take good care of yourself, Henry.

618
00:53:00,305 --> 00:53:02,140
You, too, Mr. Moses.

619
00:53:05,310 --> 00:53:06,311
Change of plan.

620
00:53:23,244 --> 00:53:24,621
Bad move, Grandpa.

621
00:53:31,294 --> 00:53:32,962
I'm back

622
00:53:35,507 --> 00:53:38,385
I'm back in the saddle again

623
00:53:39,469 --> 00:53:41,596
I'm back

624
00:53:43,390 --> 00:53:46,059
I'm back in the saddle again

625
00:53:46,142 --> 00:53:48,812
Just looks completely different
than his profile picture.

626
00:53:53,983 --> 00:53:57,654
Peeling off my boots and chaps
I'm saddle sore

627
00:53:57,737 --> 00:54:01,700
Four bits gets you time in the racks
I scream for more

628
00:54:01,783 --> 00:54:05,745
Fools' gold out of their mines
The girls are soaking wet

629
00:54:05,829 --> 00:54:10,458
Not tongue's drier than mine
I'll come when I get back

630
00:54:11,167 --> 00:54:12,252
Kordesky trained you?

631
00:54:12,377 --> 00:54:13,420
Yeah.

632
00:54:13,503 --> 00:54:15,005
I trained Kordesky.

633
00:54:17,424 --> 00:54:19,175
I'm back

634
00:54:21,177 --> 00:54:24,889
I'm back in the saddle again

635
00:54:38,737 --> 00:54:39,863
Son of a bitch!

636
00:54:45,952 --> 00:54:48,038
Seal the building. Bald, white male, 50s,

637
00:54:48,121 --> 00:54:50,582
wearing white shirt, blue pants,
shot in the shoulder.

638
00:55:00,425 --> 00:55:01,468
We should go.

639
00:55:02,218 --> 00:55:03,303
We should go now.

640
00:55:31,206 --> 00:55:33,625
I've got checkpoints at every exit.
What about the fire?

641
00:55:33,750 --> 00:55:36,336
Shut off the alarm.
I told you, there is no fire!

642
00:55:38,630 --> 00:55:41,007
-We need to evacuate.
-No, this is just a diversion.

643
00:55:41,091 --> 00:55:42,801
You make sure everyone gets checked.

644
00:55:44,719 --> 00:55:48,264
Help, help! Please come!

645
00:55:48,890 --> 00:55:50,725
I can't stop the bleeding.

646
00:55:55,522 --> 00:55:56,606
You okay, sir?

647
00:55:57,023 --> 00:55:58,108
Make a hole!

648
00:55:58,566 --> 00:55:59,901
Make a hole!

649
00:56:00,318 --> 00:56:02,654
Hold it. Let me see him.

650
00:56:03,905 --> 00:56:04,948
It's not him.

651
00:56:07,951 --> 00:56:09,077
Yeah, yeah. Go ahead.

652
00:56:09,536 --> 00:56:11,037
Fellas, help me out, here.

653
00:56:29,723 --> 00:56:30,932
Marvin?

654
00:56:37,147 --> 00:56:39,399
There's still something wrong
with this guy's head, Frank.

655
00:56:45,822 --> 00:56:47,449
You're really something, Joe.

656
00:56:48,324 --> 00:56:49,492
Marvin, you okay?

657
00:56:49,659 --> 00:56:51,161
I don't want to talk about it.

658
00:56:53,830 --> 00:56:56,124
Joe? Joe who was dead Joe?

659
00:56:57,000 --> 00:56:58,543
-She with us?
-Yeah.

660
00:56:59,878 --> 00:57:01,046
Not dead.

661
00:57:03,214 --> 00:57:04,341
Just retired.

662
00:57:10,305 --> 00:57:11,765
I guess calling wasn't an option?

663
00:57:11,848 --> 00:57:13,683
-Can we go?
-Yeah!

664
00:57:13,850 --> 00:57:15,060
You let yourself get shot?

665
00:57:15,935 --> 00:57:17,103
God damn it.

666
00:57:18,605 --> 00:57:19,773
Out.

667
00:57:20,732 --> 00:57:22,150
-You okay?
-Thanks, Doc.

668
00:57:22,484 --> 00:57:23,651
What did he get?

669
00:57:26,863 --> 00:57:28,615
I have no idea.

670
00:57:29,366 --> 00:57:33,703
You just had your ass handed
to you by a goddamn retiree.

671
00:57:35,789 --> 00:57:37,165
What did he do?

672
00:57:39,417 --> 00:57:41,878
What did Moses do to earn a lethal finding?

673
00:57:41,961 --> 00:57:44,172
I have not been read into it.

674
00:57:44,756 --> 00:57:47,384
I like you, Cooper.
You're ambitious and you get results,

675
00:57:47,592 --> 00:57:50,512
but someone just kicked in
the front door of our house,

676
00:57:50,595 --> 00:57:52,722
so you better get your shit straight.

677
00:57:53,056 --> 00:57:55,392
Nothing in your mission is changed.

678
00:57:58,311 --> 00:57:59,813
You're still bleeding.

679
00:58:00,563 --> 00:58:02,399
Must have nicked something in there.

680
00:58:02,732 --> 00:58:04,317
This is so bad.

681
00:58:04,401 --> 00:58:07,404
It's not that bad.
People get shot all the time.

682
00:58:07,487 --> 00:58:09,781
No, they don't, they get paper cuts.

683
00:58:09,906 --> 00:58:11,116
I mostly get shot.

684
00:58:11,199 --> 00:58:14,160
We're gonna have to find somebody
to plug this leak.

685
00:58:19,207 --> 00:58:20,917
Could go to Eagle's Nest.

686
00:58:22,585 --> 00:58:23,962
Then we all get shot.

687
00:58:25,588 --> 00:58:27,090
I'll just go in by myself.

688
00:58:28,049 --> 00:58:29,092
Want a vest?

689
00:58:32,178 --> 00:58:33,722
Wouldn't do any good.

690
00:59:10,300 --> 00:59:11,634
Frank Moses.

691
00:59:12,927 --> 00:59:14,262
Hi, Victoria.

692
00:59:19,351 --> 00:59:20,935
Are you here to kill me?

693
00:59:22,145 --> 00:59:23,229
No.

694
00:59:27,400 --> 00:59:28,651
You've been shot.

695
00:59:37,118 --> 00:59:39,579
Tell Marvin to stand down
before he gets hurt.

696
00:59:49,756 --> 00:59:51,007
Who's the girl?

697
00:59:51,508 --> 00:59:52,509
She's with me.

698
00:59:52,842 --> 00:59:54,511
-Vicky.
-Joe!

699
00:59:54,594 --> 00:59:57,555
Oh, Vicky. Sexy as ever.

700
00:59:59,516 --> 01:00:02,519
You old snake charmer.

701
01:00:02,811 --> 01:00:06,523
Sarah, this is Victoria.
Best wet work asset in the business.

702
01:00:06,731 --> 01:00:09,109
And a true artist with an RPN.

703
01:00:09,234 --> 01:00:10,735
What's that?

704
01:00:12,320 --> 01:00:13,863
I kill people, dear.

705
01:00:17,117 --> 01:00:18,326
You were lucky.

706
01:00:25,375 --> 01:00:26,835
How'd you do it?

707
01:00:27,544 --> 01:00:30,171
-What?
-How'd you make the transition?

708
01:00:30,672 --> 01:00:33,842
Here you seem so calm. At ease.

709
01:00:35,051 --> 01:00:36,344
I love it.

710
01:00:36,845 --> 01:00:40,932
I love it here. I love the baking.
I love the flower arranging.

711
01:00:41,558 --> 01:00:43,059
I like the routine.

712
01:00:47,564 --> 01:00:48,565
Well...

713
01:00:49,441 --> 01:00:52,610
I do get a bit restless sometimes.

714
01:00:56,448 --> 01:00:59,617
I take the odd contract on the side.

715
01:01:02,579 --> 01:01:03,663
I just can't stop.

716
01:01:05,206 --> 01:01:08,626
Yeah. Tell me about it.

717
01:01:08,710 --> 01:01:11,171
You can't just flip a switch
and become someone else.

718
01:01:11,421 --> 01:01:12,797
Put some pressure on it.

719
01:01:16,009 --> 01:01:17,427
So...

720
01:01:18,845 --> 01:01:20,388
Tell me about your lady friend.

721
01:01:22,515 --> 01:01:24,809
Makes me think that I could actually

722
01:01:29,272 --> 01:01:30,482
have a life.

723
01:01:31,608 --> 01:01:32,817
A real life.

724
01:01:32,942 --> 01:01:36,196
Oh, Francis, you're such a romantic.

725
01:01:36,446 --> 01:01:37,530
What?

726
01:01:37,614 --> 01:01:39,866
A romantic.
It's why I've always been so fond of you.

727
01:01:39,949 --> 01:01:40,950
Victoria...

728
01:01:41,034 --> 01:01:43,703
You're all hard on the outside,
but you are...

729
01:01:44,704 --> 01:01:46,664
You are gooey on the inside.

730
01:01:49,751 --> 01:01:51,127
Gooey.

731
01:01:52,879 --> 01:01:57,217
The entire back half of the Guatemala file
has been blacked out.

732
01:01:57,967 --> 01:02:02,055
But there's a list. 11 names.
Plus one that's been redacted.

733
01:02:02,430 --> 01:02:04,849
All dead. Except for Frank and Marvin.

734
01:02:05,141 --> 01:02:07,852
All the names on the reporter's list
are in the file, too,

735
01:02:07,936 --> 01:02:09,854
but she has an additional name.

736
01:02:10,313 --> 01:02:11,481
Alexander Dunning.

737
01:02:12,148 --> 01:02:13,733
Somebody's protecting him.

738
01:02:14,567 --> 01:02:18,279
Dunning is the CEO of Browning-Orvis.

739
01:02:18,446 --> 01:02:19,489
Gangsters.

740
01:02:19,989 --> 01:02:21,074
Defense contractor.

741
01:02:21,491 --> 01:02:22,534
Very connected.

742
01:02:24,035 --> 01:02:27,163
If the CIA is protecting him,

743
01:02:27,747 --> 01:02:29,374
he's under surveillance.

744
01:02:29,708 --> 01:02:30,792
We could go see him.

745
01:02:31,001 --> 01:02:32,335
You're not going without me.

746
01:02:32,836 --> 01:02:33,837
Well...

747
01:02:34,546 --> 01:02:37,674
We're getting the band back together.
That's nice.

748
01:03:02,365 --> 01:03:03,408
Yeah?

749
01:03:03,533 --> 01:03:06,036
We just got a tip. RED has a new target.

750
01:03:06,703 --> 01:03:07,704
A tip?

751
01:03:08,788 --> 01:03:09,998
FBI's on the scene.

752
01:03:10,165 --> 01:03:11,499
I'm on my way.

753
01:03:23,219 --> 01:03:26,222
The FBI has a lookout position
on the east perimeter.

754
01:03:26,931 --> 01:03:28,016
{Y:i}Copy that.

755
01:03:51,748 --> 01:03:53,249
Alexander Dunning.

756
01:03:53,375 --> 01:03:56,086
Pleasure to see you, Secretary Baptiste.

757
01:03:56,169 --> 01:03:57,962
The pleasure is with me.

758
01:04:02,842 --> 01:04:04,094
They're in.

759
01:04:05,887 --> 01:04:07,764
Frank said you wanted me with you.

760
01:04:08,098 --> 01:04:10,892
Yes, I thought it might be nice
to have a bit of girl time together.

761
01:04:12,560 --> 01:04:13,937
Get to know each other.

762
01:04:15,772 --> 01:04:20,235
And I just wanted to tell you that
in all the years I've known Francis,

763
01:04:21,277 --> 01:04:22,779
I've never seen him like this.

764
01:04:25,657 --> 01:04:27,575
So if you break his heart,

765
01:04:27,784 --> 01:04:29,244
I will kill you.

766
01:04:29,744 --> 01:04:31,579
And bury your body in the woods.

767
01:04:35,500 --> 01:04:36,835
Okay.

768
01:04:39,671 --> 01:04:41,631
Oh, this is gonna be fun.

769
01:04:45,844 --> 01:04:47,846
{Y:i}Here at Browning-Orvis,

770
01:04:48,138 --> 01:04:52,183
{Y:i}we have a longstanding commitment
to humanitarian causes

771
01:04:52,350 --> 01:04:56,813
{Y:i}because exemplary corporate citizenship
is our highest calling.

772
01:04:57,105 --> 01:05:00,692
As a company with global reach
and global interests,

773
01:05:00,775 --> 01:05:03,820
we have global responsibilities.

774
01:05:05,071 --> 01:05:06,573
Now sometimes I'm asked,

775
01:05:06,781 --> 01:05:10,994
if this commitment to ethical behavior
affects the bottom line.

776
01:05:11,202 --> 01:05:13,997
And my answer is always the same.

777
01:05:14,205 --> 01:05:15,248
Yes.

778
01:05:15,874 --> 01:05:17,917
It makes it stronger.

779
01:05:18,126 --> 01:05:22,130
This is my safe room.
Sound-proofed. Reinforced.

780
01:05:22,422 --> 01:05:24,215
Swept for bugs daily.

781
01:05:24,507 --> 01:05:26,051
You could fire a gun in here.

782
01:05:26,634 --> 01:05:28,011
No one would ever know.

783
01:05:28,678 --> 01:05:30,096
Mr. Dunning.

784
01:05:31,681 --> 01:05:35,352
I cannot imagine a more perfect place
to conduct our business.

785
01:05:39,230 --> 01:05:41,316
You do know that there's

786
01:05:42,192 --> 01:05:43,234
a surcharge

787
01:05:43,985 --> 01:05:45,820
for any arms deliveries

788
01:05:46,279 --> 01:05:49,366
to countries that are embargoed
by the United Nations.

789
01:05:50,742 --> 01:05:52,702
For every problem, monsieur,

790
01:05:53,703 --> 01:05:55,121
there is a solution.

791
01:05:59,542 --> 01:06:01,086
Excuse me.

792
01:06:06,716 --> 01:06:07,884
What are...

793
01:06:08,218 --> 01:06:11,304
{Y:i}How many CEOs can say that?

794
01:06:12,138 --> 01:06:13,890
So how did you guys meet?

795
01:06:15,183 --> 01:06:17,352
We started talking on the phone.

796
01:06:18,895 --> 01:06:21,606
I guess I liked that it wasn't real.

797
01:06:23,400 --> 01:06:24,484
Of course now I'm a fugitive,

798
01:06:24,567 --> 01:06:27,278
the CIA wants to kill me
and I'm hiding in a hole.

799
01:06:29,072 --> 01:06:32,409
I was in love with an agent once.

800
01:06:33,576 --> 01:06:34,911
What happened?

801
01:06:36,246 --> 01:06:38,331
Well, I was with MI6.

802
01:06:38,540 --> 01:06:40,375
And the relationship wasn't...

803
01:06:40,917 --> 01:06:42,544
sanctioned.

804
01:06:44,754 --> 01:06:47,799
So when it came to light,
my loyalty was questioned.

805
01:06:47,924 --> 01:06:49,426
And I was ordered to kill him.

806
01:06:50,010 --> 01:06:51,219
It was a test.

807
01:06:52,262 --> 01:06:53,763
What did you do?

808
01:06:55,390 --> 01:06:57,642
I put three bullets in his chest.

809
01:06:58,476 --> 01:06:59,686
Okay.

810
01:07:01,646 --> 01:07:03,356
Who the hell are you guys?

811
01:07:03,565 --> 01:07:04,899
You don't remember us?

812
01:07:06,109 --> 01:07:07,277
We remember you.

813
01:07:08,737 --> 01:07:12,115
You're the guy whose shit we cleaned up
down in Guatemala in 1981.

814
01:07:15,201 --> 01:07:18,997
And the question is,
who did you fly out of there?

815
01:07:19,414 --> 01:07:22,876
You don't have any idea
what you're getting into.

816
01:07:24,544 --> 01:07:25,920
First of all,

817
01:07:26,421 --> 01:07:27,589
you can't touch me.

818
01:07:27,839 --> 01:07:29,007
Sure, we can.

819
01:07:40,935 --> 01:07:42,354
Oh, yeah.

820
01:07:42,562 --> 01:07:43,772
Where'd you get this?

821
01:07:43,980 --> 01:07:45,315
Home Depot.

822
01:07:45,565 --> 01:07:48,109
-How much?
-Ten bucks.

823
01:07:48,985 --> 01:07:50,904
You want nuts?

824
01:07:51,112 --> 01:07:52,405
Nipples?

825
01:07:52,614 --> 01:07:53,656
Potty trainer?

826
01:07:54,532 --> 01:07:55,825
All right, stop it.

827
01:07:56,034 --> 01:07:57,077
Nuts.

828
01:07:57,994 --> 01:08:01,039
Stop it. For the love of Christ, stop it!

829
01:08:01,122 --> 01:08:02,499
Stop already!

830
01:08:04,501 --> 01:08:05,669
Now you got something to say?

831
01:08:09,047 --> 01:08:12,300
We extracted a young lieutenant

832
01:08:12,509 --> 01:08:15,428
who is the son of the late Senator,

833
01:08:15,887 --> 01:08:18,014
James Stanton.

834
01:08:22,185 --> 01:08:23,353
Robert Stanton?

835
01:08:23,561 --> 01:08:25,814
Vice President of the United States.

836
01:08:26,064 --> 01:08:29,818
You're saying the Vice President
killed all the people in that village?

837
01:08:29,901 --> 01:08:32,696
Yeah. Went completely off the reservation.

838
01:08:32,821 --> 01:08:34,823
And that New York Times reporter?

839
01:08:35,490 --> 01:08:36,658
Did she pressure you?

840
01:08:36,825 --> 01:08:39,244
Yeah. She called me. Twice.

841
01:08:39,953 --> 01:08:41,413
So I called the V.P.

842
01:08:41,579 --> 01:08:44,416
And what did you think
would happen then?

843
01:08:44,582 --> 01:08:46,042
Oh, whatever.

844
01:08:46,626 --> 01:08:48,211
I made him Vice President.

845
01:08:48,503 --> 01:08:52,507
You kept your mouth shut
and the Stantons made you rich.

846
01:08:52,590 --> 01:08:53,675
{Y:i}Been working with

847
01:08:53,758 --> 01:08:54,801
{Y:i}our partners in the developing world

848
01:08:54,884 --> 01:08:56,344
{Y:i}to root out corruption and...

849
01:08:59,222 --> 01:09:00,306
Okay.

850
01:09:02,392 --> 01:09:05,228
I will pay whatever it costs

851
01:09:05,729 --> 01:09:07,188
to get rid of this thing.

852
01:09:08,565 --> 01:09:10,442
We're not here for your money, home.

853
01:09:10,650 --> 01:09:14,279
We're here because that New York Times
reporter had the list of names

854
01:09:14,487 --> 01:09:16,698
of everybody who was in Guatemala.

855
01:09:16,906 --> 01:09:19,993
And everybody on that list
has been ordered killed.

856
01:09:20,201 --> 01:09:21,327
Except you.

857
01:09:22,954 --> 01:09:24,622
I had nothing to do with that.

858
01:09:26,541 --> 01:09:28,209
Don't you see?

859
01:09:28,710 --> 01:09:33,798
He's trying to clean up his past
and get rid of me in one shot.

860
01:09:34,257 --> 01:09:37,677
He's trying to cut me loose
before he runs for President.

861
01:09:37,927 --> 01:09:39,971
{Y:i}We have some
major activity out here.

862
01:09:40,555 --> 01:09:41,681
{Y:i}Looks like we're blown.

863
01:09:58,239 --> 01:10:00,950
We're in position.
Perimeter's set. No one's getting out.

864
01:10:05,121 --> 01:10:06,790
They're moving a team up the east side.

865
01:10:06,998 --> 01:10:08,416
Are you gonna let me talk to them?

866
01:10:08,500 --> 01:10:10,543
I can negotiate something.

867
01:10:10,710 --> 01:10:13,505
Thanks, when we want your help,
we'll get out the drain cleaner.

868
01:10:13,713 --> 01:10:15,799
Listen, Plastic Man,

869
01:10:15,882 --> 01:10:19,386
those bastards out there
probably have orders to kill me, too.

870
01:10:19,594 --> 01:10:20,637
I hope so.

871
01:10:20,845 --> 01:10:24,265
Why? 'Cause I'm a bad guy?

872
01:10:25,016 --> 01:10:26,434
I'm scum?

873
01:10:26,643 --> 01:10:28,103
Can I just shoot him now?

874
01:10:28,311 --> 01:10:29,479
No.

875
01:10:29,688 --> 01:10:32,148
You don't have people killed.

876
01:10:32,399 --> 01:10:36,820
I have people killed,
I'm the bad guy. Remember?

877
01:10:42,367 --> 01:10:43,827
Not worth a bullet.

878
01:10:52,043 --> 01:10:53,128
Hello?

879
01:10:53,420 --> 01:10:54,587
How's retirement, Frank?

880
01:10:55,088 --> 01:10:56,673
It's been a real blast.

881
01:10:56,798 --> 01:10:59,217
If we have to come in there and get you,
it's gonna be messy.

882
01:10:59,592 --> 01:11:02,095
You bet. Real messy.

883
01:11:02,554 --> 01:11:04,097
I've got my orders, Frank.

884
01:11:04,472 --> 01:11:06,016
They come from the Vice President.

885
01:11:06,307 --> 01:11:09,978
He's ordered these hits to cover up
the war crimes he committed in Guatemala.

886
01:11:10,186 --> 01:11:11,646
I find that hard to believe.

887
01:11:11,855 --> 01:11:13,857
How did you know you'd find me here?

888
01:11:13,940 --> 01:11:16,276
Some anonymous untraceable tip?

889
01:11:18,445 --> 01:11:20,030
Here's the deal, Frank.

890
01:11:20,572 --> 01:11:23,366
You're gonna walk out that front door
and give yourself up.

891
01:11:23,575 --> 01:11:25,744
You have my word no one will shoot you.

892
01:11:25,952 --> 01:11:29,581
I'll personally take you in and
you will get to tell your side of the story.

893
01:11:30,248 --> 01:11:32,417
You got 60 seconds to decide.

894
01:11:36,588 --> 01:11:37,589
What's it look like?

895
01:11:37,672 --> 01:11:39,215
There's no clean exit.

896
01:11:39,841 --> 01:11:41,801
They seem to be coming from everywhere.

897
01:11:48,016 --> 01:11:50,393
If we had a distraction,
I could cover you to the woods.

898
01:12:03,239 --> 01:12:05,867
Looks like there's not a lot of options, kid.

899
01:12:08,953 --> 01:12:10,038
I mean

900
01:12:12,040 --> 01:12:14,167
somebody's gonna have to make
the hard choice

901
01:12:14,250 --> 01:12:15,585
if weâre gonna get out of here alive.

902
01:12:30,433 --> 01:12:31,768
Been wild.

903
01:12:34,354 --> 01:12:36,064
Wild and crazy.

904
01:12:37,232 --> 01:12:39,609
But I wouldn't want it any other way.

905
01:12:46,866 --> 01:12:48,284
An honor.

906
01:12:55,458 --> 01:12:56,793
Good luck.

907
01:13:06,052 --> 01:13:07,470
Tell your men to hold their fire.

908
01:13:07,929 --> 01:13:09,014
I'm coming out.

909
01:13:10,890 --> 01:13:13,476
He's coming out. All units, hold fire.

910
01:13:13,560 --> 01:13:15,562
Repeat, all units, hold fire.

911
01:13:15,812 --> 01:13:16,980
Roger that.

912
01:13:22,527 --> 01:13:23,820
Get behind.

913
01:13:25,488 --> 01:13:27,490
Come out now. I've got you covered.

914
01:13:44,382 --> 01:13:45,550
Who fired the shot?

915
01:14:11,368 --> 01:14:13,578
Tell me when the boys make cover,
we'll move.

916
01:14:15,580 --> 01:14:16,623
Now.

917
01:14:53,118 --> 01:14:54,703
They've got Sarah.

918
01:14:58,206 --> 01:14:59,874
Frank, you're no good to her dead.

919
01:15:00,083 --> 01:15:01,292
We gotta move.

920
01:15:04,379 --> 01:15:05,463
Come!

921
01:15:06,589 --> 01:15:08,675
Now is not time to waste.

922
01:15:09,300 --> 01:15:10,468
Ivan?

923
01:15:14,180 --> 01:15:16,474
It's nice to see you again, Ivan.

924
01:15:16,558 --> 01:15:17,934
Did he just call you "bunny"?

925
01:15:20,687 --> 01:15:22,564
Life sometimes is complicated.

926
01:15:30,739 --> 01:15:32,073
To Joe.

927
01:15:34,409 --> 01:15:35,744
Joe.

928
01:15:46,296 --> 01:15:49,424
Not to push the bounds of propriety,

929
01:15:49,632 --> 01:15:51,384
but don't you think
we ought to discuss the fact that

930
01:15:51,468 --> 01:15:55,263
the CIA's being used by the Vice President
as his personal hit squad

931
01:15:55,347 --> 01:15:58,683
and that they'll do whatever they can
to find us and kill us?

932
01:16:00,852 --> 01:16:02,103
Options?

933
01:16:04,189 --> 01:16:05,774
We could go public.

934
01:16:05,982 --> 01:16:10,278
Yeah, right.
That didn't work very well for the reporter.

935
01:16:10,528 --> 01:16:12,405
And what about Frank's girlfriend?

936
01:16:12,697 --> 01:16:14,199
They'll kill her so fast.

937
01:16:14,991 --> 01:16:18,536
First they'll interrogate her.
They probably already got the wires.

938
01:16:18,620 --> 01:16:21,873
Then give her a little snorkel.
Give her a jump.

939
01:16:22,082 --> 01:16:23,667
-Bring in the dent.
-Marvin!

940
01:16:25,377 --> 01:16:28,296
God! You are such an idiot.

941
01:16:41,851 --> 01:16:43,186
I want to show you something.

942
01:16:51,027 --> 01:16:52,904
This was done to me by the love of my life.

943
01:16:54,531 --> 01:16:57,033
It seems that what we had
was not meant to be.

944
01:16:58,159 --> 01:17:00,453
But now she sits

945
01:17:01,246 --> 01:17:03,373
outside my house

946
01:17:04,874 --> 01:17:06,918
drinking vodka.

947
01:17:11,172 --> 01:17:13,550
Three bullets in the chest.

948
01:17:14,259 --> 01:17:17,137
When I woke alive,

949
01:17:19,097 --> 01:17:21,099
I knew she still loved me.

950
01:17:21,683 --> 01:17:24,227
Or else it would have been the head.

951
01:17:25,478 --> 01:17:28,148
It was big risk for her, of course,

952
01:17:28,940 --> 01:17:33,403
but one does crazy things for love.

953
01:17:36,448 --> 01:17:39,409
Do not fear for your love, my friend.

954
01:17:40,076 --> 01:17:42,412
With a small dedicated group,

955
01:17:42,746 --> 01:17:45,415
there is nothing
that cannot be accomplished.

956
01:17:46,708 --> 01:17:48,043
Let me be blunt.

957
01:17:48,460 --> 01:17:51,421
Nobody knows you're here. You don't exist.

958
01:17:52,213 --> 01:17:53,965
And unless you cooperate fully,

959
01:17:54,466 --> 01:17:56,426
there's nothing I can't do to you.

960
01:17:56,926 --> 01:17:58,928
-Sir.
-Not now.

961
01:17:59,012 --> 01:18:00,764
Moses is on the phone.

962
01:18:02,849 --> 01:18:04,642
Okay. Trace is running.

963
01:18:10,607 --> 01:18:11,649
Moses.

964
01:18:12,150 --> 01:18:13,568
Here's the thing, Cooper.

965
01:18:15,028 --> 01:18:18,281
With age comes a certain perspective.

966
01:18:18,406 --> 01:18:22,869
I'd be a liar if I said there wasn't a time
when I was exactly like you.

967
01:18:23,411 --> 01:18:24,746
Blind ambition.

968
01:18:25,205 --> 01:18:26,414
Misplaced trust.

969
01:18:26,623 --> 01:18:28,375
Why are you telling me this?

970
01:18:29,542 --> 01:18:31,294
It might help me to decide what to do next.

971
01:18:31,378 --> 01:18:32,462
Just keep it going.

972
01:18:32,629 --> 01:18:34,255
Why? What are you thinking about?

973
01:18:34,798 --> 01:18:36,966
Our business is a very hard one.

974
01:18:37,467 --> 01:18:38,802
But it was never

975
01:18:39,761 --> 01:18:42,013
the killing or the stress,

976
01:18:42,305 --> 01:18:43,932
or the bad pay that bothered me.

977
01:18:44,140 --> 01:18:46,142
What was it, Frank?

978
01:18:46,643 --> 01:18:49,437
It's how anything that you love

979
01:18:50,313 --> 01:18:51,523
can be taken away from you.

980
01:18:52,816 --> 01:18:54,609
It taught me never to care.

981
01:18:54,984 --> 01:18:56,152
Never to invest.

982
01:18:57,862 --> 01:18:59,656
Then I met this woman.

983
01:19:00,490 --> 01:19:01,825
Sarah.

984
01:19:04,202 --> 01:19:05,704
And now you have her.

985
01:19:06,329 --> 01:19:09,290
Now I can't think of anything
more horrible

986
01:19:09,499 --> 01:19:13,169
than to know that your enemies
can hurt someone that you love.

987
01:19:13,628 --> 01:19:16,506
The feeling is almost indescribable.

988
01:19:22,721 --> 01:19:24,139
You still there, Cooper?

989
01:19:26,099 --> 01:19:27,350
You're at my house.

990
01:19:35,859 --> 01:19:37,777
Almost indescribable, isn't it?

991
01:19:40,697 --> 01:19:41,781
Please.

992
01:19:43,825 --> 01:19:45,285
Please don't hurt my family.

993
01:19:46,494 --> 01:19:48,204
If anything happens to Sarah,

994
01:19:49,330 --> 01:19:51,541
I will rip everything you love
out of your life.

995
01:19:53,084 --> 01:19:54,502
And then I'll kill you.

996
01:19:56,963 --> 01:19:59,049
I swear to you, I will keep Sarah safe.

997
01:19:59,591 --> 01:20:01,217
We don't have much time.

998
01:20:01,426 --> 01:20:02,761
Do you understand that?

999
01:20:06,056 --> 01:20:07,432
What are you gonna do, Frank?

1000
01:20:08,224 --> 01:20:10,101
I'm gonna kill the Vice President.

1001
01:20:10,602 --> 01:20:11,936
What are you gonna do?

1002
01:20:19,027 --> 01:20:20,236
Move! Move!

1003
01:20:26,493 --> 01:20:27,619
Mom!

1004
01:21:35,437 --> 01:21:36,771
Frank left this for me.

1005
01:21:38,940 --> 01:21:40,483
Where did he get it from?

1006
01:21:42,027 --> 01:21:45,155
The secure records depository of the CIA.

1007
01:21:55,832 --> 01:21:57,667
Look, Sarah.

1008
01:21:59,627 --> 01:22:02,005
I know Frank's been right
about a few things.

1009
01:22:03,048 --> 01:22:06,217
But he's about to cross a line
from which there's no turning back.

1010
01:22:07,218 --> 01:22:10,847
Right now,
you have an opportunity to help him.

1011
01:22:12,015 --> 01:22:14,225
You need to tell me everything you know.

1012
01:22:14,684 --> 01:22:16,686
Because if I can't stop him,

1013
01:22:18,355 --> 01:22:19,606
I'm gonna have to kill him.

1014
01:22:26,821 --> 01:22:30,492
Do you know who Frank Moses is?
I mean, really is?

1015
01:22:31,284 --> 01:22:33,244
Do you know what he's done?

1016
01:22:39,542 --> 01:22:41,961
You're asking me for help? That is so lame.

1017
01:22:44,047 --> 01:22:45,840
He's gonna eat you for lunch.

1018
01:22:52,972 --> 01:22:54,224
She's never gonna trust us.

1019
01:22:54,599 --> 01:22:57,227
I can't blame her. The tip off was a trap.

1020
01:22:57,435 --> 01:22:59,729
Someone's got us dancing like marionettes.

1021
01:23:05,402 --> 01:23:07,529
Just like Moses called it.

1022
01:23:08,405 --> 01:23:09,531
Yeah.

1023
01:23:11,533 --> 01:23:13,118
He will take a shot at the V.P.

1024
01:23:13,868 --> 01:23:15,912
That's a problem for the Secret Service.

1025
01:23:18,581 --> 01:23:20,834
Moses'll take them apart.

1026
01:23:22,419 --> 01:23:23,586
Plug me into their detail.

1027
01:23:25,380 --> 01:23:26,715
You got it.

1028
01:23:27,549 --> 01:23:28,633
What about her?

1029
01:23:29,592 --> 01:23:32,887
I'll keep her close. Protected. Off the grid.

1030
01:23:40,103 --> 01:23:41,312
I put a few things away.

1031
01:23:42,105 --> 01:23:43,606
Just in case.

1032
01:23:43,732 --> 01:23:44,733
Frank.

1033
01:23:50,488 --> 01:23:52,240
Swedish K.

1034
01:23:54,159 --> 01:23:56,745
Now that is exciting.

1035
01:23:59,164 --> 01:24:00,248
Explosives?

1036
01:24:00,749 --> 01:24:01,958
Just past the RPGs.

1037
01:24:02,751 --> 01:24:03,793
I love you, man.

1038
01:24:04,461 --> 01:24:07,422
-Make yourself at home.
-The Vice President's gonna love this.

1039
01:24:20,018 --> 01:24:21,603
Nice to see you, too.

1040
01:24:57,389 --> 01:24:58,431
Thank you.

1041
01:25:07,565 --> 01:25:08,692
Oh. I'm sorry.

1042
01:25:09,442 --> 01:25:11,861
Sorry. Silly.

1043
01:25:14,698 --> 01:25:15,740
Thank you, ma'am.

1044
01:25:29,212 --> 01:25:31,589
-Thank you very much.
-You're welcome.

1045
01:25:39,889 --> 01:25:41,725
Welcome, Ms. Brown.

1046
01:25:44,102 --> 01:25:46,354
It's a pleasure to have you
at our Victory Fund Gala.

1047
01:25:46,604 --> 01:25:48,565
Oh, I'm so looking forward to it.

1048
01:25:53,528 --> 01:25:54,904
Raptor is cleared for entry.

1049
01:25:55,739 --> 01:25:57,407
After you, Mr. Vice President.

1050
01:25:57,615 --> 01:26:02,412
{Y:i}A true war hero,
a fabulous friend and a wonderful leader.

1051
01:26:02,996 --> 01:26:06,458
{Y:i}And so it's with great pleasure
I introduce to you,

1052
01:26:07,083 --> 01:26:09,210
vice President Robert Stanton.

1053
01:26:12,672 --> 01:26:14,090
I love you, sir!

1054
01:26:17,761 --> 01:26:20,764
Thank you, everybody.
Thank you so much for being here.

1055
01:26:21,097 --> 01:26:22,432
I'm gonna keep this short and sweet

1056
01:26:22,515 --> 01:26:24,684
so you'll actually write those checks
you've been promising.

1057
01:26:29,064 --> 01:26:31,024
Seriously, though, great to see you all.

1058
01:26:32,776 --> 01:26:34,235
It's the wonderful people here tonight

1059
01:26:34,319 --> 01:26:36,071
that got us into the White House
in the first place.

1060
01:26:36,154 --> 01:26:38,365
And I believe
it's this wonderful group of people

1061
01:26:38,448 --> 01:26:41,576
who will keep us there
for a long, long time!

1062
01:26:43,995 --> 01:26:45,789
My good friends,

1063
01:26:46,081 --> 01:26:48,708
I am proud to announce that I will
be forming an exploratory committee

1064
01:26:48,792 --> 01:26:52,379
with the primary goal of seeking
a nomination for the Presidency.

1065
01:27:02,180 --> 01:27:05,141
We've had a great journey together.

1066
01:27:05,308 --> 01:27:09,354
But I firmly believe
that the best is still to come.

1067
01:27:10,313 --> 01:27:11,690
God bless you all.

1068
01:27:12,148 --> 01:27:13,775
God bless America!

1069
01:27:38,133 --> 01:27:39,509
Hello, bunny.

1070
01:27:39,926 --> 01:27:42,095
Moves like that could get you killed.

1071
01:27:42,804 --> 01:27:46,391
Your radiance tonight
renders me almost speechless.

1072
01:27:46,474 --> 01:27:47,517
Almost.

1073
01:27:51,688 --> 01:27:53,064
What are you grinning at?

1074
01:27:53,940 --> 01:27:57,235
I've always dreamed
of killing an American President.

1075
01:27:57,402 --> 01:27:58,528
Vice President.

1076
01:27:59,029 --> 01:28:00,030
Whatever.

1077
01:28:01,364 --> 01:28:05,243
Having you in my arms once again,
I get carried away.

1078
01:28:05,493 --> 01:28:06,536
Really?

1079
01:28:09,039 --> 01:28:10,331
Tell me you love me.

1080
01:28:12,042 --> 01:28:13,960
It's been a long time, Ivan.

1081
01:28:14,544 --> 01:28:15,795
Blink of an eye.

1082
01:28:18,923 --> 01:28:20,467
Ivan.

1083
01:28:20,550 --> 01:28:22,385
The music has stopped.

1084
01:28:23,345 --> 01:28:24,554
Is it?

1085
01:28:27,891 --> 01:28:29,225
To work then.

1086
01:28:35,565 --> 01:28:36,691
Ivan!

1087
01:28:51,790 --> 01:28:53,124
Do you smell that?

1088
01:29:15,855 --> 01:29:18,066
-This area is off limits.
-No, it's fine. It's fine.

1089
01:29:18,274 --> 01:29:19,401
You'll have to turn around.

1090
01:29:19,526 --> 01:29:21,111
No, it's fine.

1091
01:29:21,569 --> 01:29:23,321
It's all right. I'm sure I'm allowed.

1092
01:29:23,405 --> 01:29:26,491
You'll have to go back up, ma'am,
or I'll have to treat you as a threat.

1093
01:29:26,574 --> 01:29:27,951
Where exactly is the threat?

1094
01:29:47,554 --> 01:29:49,014
Good to see you.

1095
01:29:49,097 --> 01:29:50,390
Oh, my God!

1096
01:29:50,974 --> 01:29:53,476
Gas! I smell gas!

1097
01:29:53,560 --> 01:29:55,937
Gas! Gas!

1098
01:29:56,312 --> 01:29:57,355
Gas!

1099
01:30:07,323 --> 01:30:08,533
Stand aside.

1100
01:30:11,327 --> 01:30:13,288
Primary exit blocked. Secondary, move.

1101
01:30:13,371 --> 01:30:14,998
Move! Move! Move!

1102
01:30:19,794 --> 01:30:22,047
Let me out of here!
Let me out of here!

1103
01:31:04,047 --> 01:31:05,173
Go.

1104
01:31:08,051 --> 01:31:09,386
What the hell are they using?

1105
01:31:30,699 --> 01:31:33,076
Get back up in here
to the north stairwell, now!

1106
01:31:52,595 --> 01:31:54,014
Ah, yes.

1107
01:32:03,648 --> 01:32:05,442
Move to the other limo. I'll cover you.

1108
01:32:26,713 --> 01:32:29,049
We have to go. Now! Now!

1109
01:32:36,097 --> 01:32:37,640
Approaching target from the rear.

1110
01:33:03,333 --> 01:33:04,584
Outside!

1111
01:33:05,669 --> 01:33:07,087
Secret Service,
everybody down!

1112
01:33:31,986 --> 01:33:33,113
Cover us! We're moving now!

1113
01:33:35,240 --> 01:33:36,866
Come on! Move!

1114
01:33:36,991 --> 01:33:37,992
Go!

1115
01:33:43,456 --> 01:33:46,209
I remember
the Secret Service being tougher.

1116
01:33:46,292 --> 01:33:47,460
Me, too.

1117
01:33:50,588 --> 01:33:52,132
-Okay?
-Yeah.

1118
01:34:00,181 --> 01:34:01,391
Marvin.

1119
01:34:04,477 --> 01:34:05,729
Bugger!

1120
01:34:36,217 --> 01:34:37,635
-Almost there.
-Marvin.

1121
01:34:37,886 --> 01:34:38,970
We gotta move.

1122
01:34:39,596 --> 01:34:43,099
You're on your own. I'm no use anymore.

1123
01:34:44,601 --> 01:34:46,603
Good luck. Go on.

1124
01:34:50,857 --> 01:34:52,525
Let's move!

1125
01:34:54,194 --> 01:34:55,528
Are you hit, sir?

1126
01:34:55,904 --> 01:34:58,114
-Are you hit?
-I'm fine! Just get me the hell out of here.

1127
01:35:16,966 --> 01:35:20,553
Perhaps I could be of assistance?

1128
01:35:34,484 --> 01:35:35,777
I love you.

1129
01:35:36,152 --> 01:35:37,404
I know.

1130
01:35:44,828 --> 01:35:45,912
Freeze!

1131
01:35:52,460 --> 01:35:53,586
What the...

1132
01:35:57,298 --> 01:35:58,550
Go. Go!

1133
01:36:00,844 --> 01:36:01,886
Go!

1134
01:36:12,647 --> 01:36:15,150
Get in! Get in!

1135
01:36:15,859 --> 01:36:16,943
Go, go, go!

1136
01:36:21,322 --> 01:36:23,700
Stop the car! Stop...

1137
01:36:23,783 --> 01:36:25,410
Don't you dare stop! You keep going!

1138
01:36:25,493 --> 01:36:27,495
Stop the car! Pull over!

1139
01:36:35,920 --> 01:36:37,881
I wanna know
what the hell that was all about!

1140
01:36:58,276 --> 01:37:00,278
-Burbacher!
-Get him off!

1141
01:37:00,528 --> 01:37:02,072
Pull over!

1142
01:37:03,782 --> 01:37:05,617
Raptor is secure.

1143
01:37:22,509 --> 01:37:23,718
Who are you?

1144
01:37:23,927 --> 01:37:25,762
One of the men you ordered killed.

1145
01:37:27,347 --> 01:37:29,557
I don't know what you're talking about.

1146
01:37:29,933 --> 01:37:31,476
Guatemala.

1147
01:37:32,894 --> 01:37:34,187
I was there.

1148
01:37:40,735 --> 01:37:41,861
Well...

1149
01:37:47,701 --> 01:37:50,161
I'm sure we can negotiate something.

1150
01:37:50,578 --> 01:37:52,372
Starting to come back to you now, is it?

1151
01:37:54,374 --> 01:37:56,376
If you're looking for revenge...

1152
01:37:56,710 --> 01:37:58,628
This is not about revenge.

1153
01:38:03,842 --> 01:38:05,760
Are you gonna kill me?

1154
01:38:08,346 --> 01:38:09,639
Not just you.

1155
01:38:20,984 --> 01:38:22,027
Yeah?

1156
01:38:22,110 --> 01:38:24,154
I'm at the Evanston power plant.

1157
01:38:24,612 --> 01:38:26,781
You have 15 minutes to bring me Sarah.

1158
01:38:26,906 --> 01:38:29,117
Or I kill the vice President.

1159
01:38:33,413 --> 01:38:35,331
He just made contact. He wants the girl.

1160
01:38:35,415 --> 01:38:38,168
Evanston Power Station. 15 minutes.

1161
01:38:38,793 --> 01:38:40,337
You better alert Secret Service.

1162
01:38:40,545 --> 01:38:41,671
Copy that.

1163
01:38:42,630 --> 01:38:44,799
Secret Service is en route.

1164
01:39:02,359 --> 01:39:03,693
All right, come on.

1165
01:39:07,989 --> 01:39:09,324
Where's Sarah?

1166
01:39:09,657 --> 01:39:11,034
She's on her way.

1167
01:39:13,244 --> 01:39:14,913
It's over, Frank.

1168
01:39:15,538 --> 01:39:17,874
Any minute
the whole world is gonna drop on you.

1169
01:39:18,958 --> 01:39:20,293
We'll see.

1170
01:39:44,109 --> 01:39:46,569
Hey, tough guy.

1171
01:39:48,154 --> 01:39:49,656
Surprised to see me?

1172
01:39:51,324 --> 01:39:52,367
What the hell's this?

1173
01:39:52,492 --> 01:39:53,535
Alex...

1174
01:39:54,160 --> 01:39:57,747
Just give him what he wants.
I can't do this anymore.

1175
01:40:00,875 --> 01:40:02,919
You ordered these killings, not me.

1176
01:40:04,254 --> 01:40:06,548
I don't want to have
anything to do with this anymore.

1177
01:40:12,303 --> 01:40:13,763
You shot me.

1178
01:40:14,764 --> 01:40:16,182
Shut up.

1179
01:40:20,270 --> 01:40:23,106
I loved watching you being a good guy.

1180
01:40:24,357 --> 01:40:27,110
Kicking ass for your country.

1181
01:40:28,403 --> 01:40:31,364
It showed a spectacular lack of vision.

1182
01:40:32,615 --> 01:40:33,783
The girl goes free.

1183
01:40:34,617 --> 01:40:36,161
That'll cost you a gun.

1184
01:40:41,416 --> 01:40:43,126
A life for a life.

1185
01:40:47,380 --> 01:40:49,466
I tore up all those checks.

1186
01:40:50,675 --> 01:40:52,093
I know.

1187
01:40:55,472 --> 01:40:56,973
I just wanted to talk to you.

1188
01:41:04,147 --> 01:41:05,148
Cooper,

1189
01:41:06,316 --> 01:41:07,484
cuff him.

1190
01:41:20,830 --> 01:41:22,916
Wilkes told me you had promise.

1191
01:41:22,999 --> 01:41:25,293
Okay, here's how it goes.

1192
01:41:25,502 --> 01:41:28,004
Moses just shot the V.P.

1193
01:41:28,296 --> 01:41:30,423
You kill him and the girl,

1194
01:41:30,632 --> 01:41:33,176
and you're head of the CIA.

1195
01:41:35,011 --> 01:41:36,096
Cooper.

1196
01:41:38,598 --> 01:41:40,392
This is gonna happen either way.

1197
01:41:42,936 --> 01:41:44,354
Fuck you, Cynthia.

1198
01:42:42,245 --> 01:42:43,580
Thanks.

1199
01:42:48,585 --> 01:42:49,919
This gonna be a problem?

1200
01:42:53,840 --> 01:42:55,008
No.

1201
01:42:56,092 --> 01:42:57,177
I got it...

1202
01:42:58,762 --> 01:43:00,013
Grandpa.

1203
01:43:11,358 --> 01:43:12,442
Feel better now?

1204
01:43:12,734 --> 01:43:13,777
Yeah.

1205
01:43:14,444 --> 01:43:16,237
Wanna get pancakes?

1206
01:43:19,324 --> 01:43:21,993
Can you believe it? It all worked out.

1207
01:43:22,243 --> 01:43:25,663
Something bad is gonna happen very soon.

1208
01:43:26,331 --> 01:43:28,500
Maybe not. Wait a second.

1209
01:43:29,542 --> 01:43:30,919
Nobody's chasing us.

1210
01:43:32,253 --> 01:43:34,339
No one's trying to kill us.

1211
01:43:35,298 --> 01:43:37,842
I think we just got our lives back.

1212
01:43:38,802 --> 01:43:40,095
Almost.

1213
01:43:41,513 --> 01:43:43,765
You still owe me a small favor.

1214
01:43:43,848 --> 01:43:44,974
Oh, Ivan!

1215
01:43:46,142 --> 01:43:47,644
His timing is terrible.

1216
01:43:48,103 --> 01:43:50,230
You gave a favor to him?

1217
01:43:51,189 --> 01:43:54,275
Just a tiny little nuclear problem
in Moldova.

1218
01:43:56,236 --> 01:43:57,320
Can we go?

1219
01:44:01,074 --> 01:44:02,617
Yes. We can go.

1220
01:44:33,398 --> 01:44:35,692
I told you
something bad was gonna happen.

1221
01:44:35,900 --> 01:44:37,235
Keep your dress on.

1222
01:44:39,237 --> 01:44:40,905
Moldova sucks.

1223
01:44:41,114 --> 01:44:42,615
Moldova sucks!

1224
01:44:44,200 --> 01:44:46,536
Next time,
your girlfriend can wear the dress.

1225
01:44:48,538 --> 01:44:51,541
.:: Napisy24 - Nowy Wymiar Napisów ::.
Napisy24.pl
